  "description": "SERGEE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C156 H198 N8 O38 Tb6,2(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.458-4.808 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 75.34-171.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [TbIII6(μ4-O)2(μ4-CO3)2(μ-HCO2)2(5)2(dmf)8(H2O)2]·2MeOH·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Tb(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
